WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.173
YAML is often chosen because it is readable and pleasant for
configuration.

2
00:00:04.173 --> 00:00:08.803
That flexibility is useful, but it also creates security and reliability
concerns.

3
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:16.889
YAML can support richer features than many teams need, including tags,
anchors, aliases, complex types, and implementation-specific behavior.

4
00:00:16.889 --> 00:00:21.389
Secure Python code should accept only the YAML features required for the
use case.

5
00:00:21.389 --> 00:00:23.019
Safe loader concepts matter.

6
00:00:23.019 --> 00:00:33.909
When YAML comes from an untrusted or lightly trusted source, the parser
should be configured to load ordinary data rather than construct arbitrary
application objects or interpret broad behavior.

7
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:43.039
The important principle is simple: parsing a document should not silently
become object construction, privileged configuration, or executable
program behavior.

8
00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:48.712
Configuration files and user-submitted YAML should not be treated the same
just because both are YAML.

9
00:00:48.712 --> 00:00:52.886
A reviewed deployment configuration may be allowed to set runtime options.

10
00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:58.559
A customer-uploaded policy file or workflow description should be
constrained to an explicit schema.

11
00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:05.667
The application should separate trusted configuration from user data, and
it should avoid broad loaders for untrusted content.

12
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.014
Keep YAML schemas simple and predictable.

13
00:01:08.014 --> 00:01:16.361
Limit accepted features where practical, document expected keys, reject or
ignore unsupported features intentionally, and validate after parsing.

14
00:01:16.361 --> 00:01:18.578
YAML is not dangerous because it is YAML.

15
00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:28.360
Risk appears when flexible parsing is combined with unclear trust, broad
loaders, complex features, and configuration decisions that the
application did not intend to expose.
